                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Categories of Questions in the Colonial Field on
                        Which it Would be Desirable to Have Decisions Taken by a Two-Thirds
                        Majority</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d896-f1"/></p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Decisions involving the political affairs of Non-Self-Governing
                        Territories, either general or in relation to particular territories.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Decisions to admit petitions, written or oral, relating to the affairs of
                        Non-Self-Governing Territories. (Note: in general such decisions would fall
                        to be taken in the first instance in an Assembly Committee, where Article
                        18(2) is inapplicable, but we should urge reference of such questions to the
                        Plenary Assembly for decision).</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>Decisions involving reference to the International Court of Justice of a
                        Colonial (or Trusteeship) question.</item>
                    <label>4.</label>
                    <item>Decisions relating to the cessation of Article 73(<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >e</hi>) transmissions.</item>
                    <label>5.</label>
                    <item>Decisions involving recommendations to administering powers to pursue some
                        specific policy or to accept some specific obligation in relation to the
                        United Nations or Colonial questions.</item>
                    <label>6.</label>
                    <item>Decisions involving an interpretation of the scope of Chapter XI of the
                        Charter e.g. the extent to which Article 73 (<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>)
                        empowers the United Nations to examine the political affairs of
                        Non-Self-Governing Territories.</item>
                </list>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
